Subject: [PATCH 1/2] compat/wctype.h: read <wchar.h> before the iswXXX macros exist (Emscripten / musl)

musl declares iswalnum() and friends in <wchar.h> as well. When <wctype.h> (this shim) was included first, its macros rewrote those
declarations into conflicting redeclarations of ucd_isalnum() and friends, and src/libespeak-ng/dictionary.c did not compile for WebAssembly.

---
diff --git a/src/include/compat/wctype.h b/src/include/compat/wctype.h
index e0d2c64..ac23aea 100644
--- a/src/include/compat/wctype.h
+++ b/src/include/compat/wctype.h
@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@
 #include_next <wctype.h>
 #endif
 
+/* Emscripten (musl) declares iswalnum() and friends in <wchar.h> as well: that header has to be read BEFORE the macros below exist,
+ * otherwise its declarations are rewritten into conflicting redeclarations of ucd_isalnum() and friends. */
+#include <wchar.h>
+
 #include <ucd/ucd.h>
 
 #define iswalnum  ucd_isalnum
